# Infrastructure

Terraform in the repository root creates a serverless API in the Google Cloud
project `${{ values.gcpProjectId }}`, region `${{ region }}`. Resource names
start with `${{ name }}`.

## Request path

{% if directLb -%}
```text
client -> external Application Load Balancer + Cloud Armor -> Cloud Function
```

No API Gateway is created. API Gateway cannot refuse requests sent straight to
its own `gateway.dev` address, so a firewall in front of it can be bypassed.
With authentication set to `none` nothing else would stop such a request, so
the load balancer is connected to the function directly and the function
accepts requests from the load balancer only (`ALLOW_INTERNAL_AND_GCLB`). The
function is invocable by `allUsers`; an organisation policy that restricts
IAM members to your domain has to allow that for this project.
{%- elif values.enableWaf -%}
```text
client -> external Application Load Balancer + Cloud Armor -> API Gateway -> Cloud Function
```

Clients call the load balancer (`api_url` output). The connection between a
load balancer and API Gateway is a Preview feature of API Gateway.

API Gateway cannot refuse requests sent straight to its own `gateway.dev`
address (`gateway_url` output). Such requests skip Cloud Armor but still pass
the gateway's `${{ auth }}` authentication. Publish only the load balancer
address.
{%- else -%}
```text
client -> API Gateway -> Cloud Function
```
{%- endif %}

