## Deployment

### State backend

The configuration declares an empty `gcs` backend. Create a bucket for the
state once and pass it at init time:

```bash
terraform init \
  -backend-config="bucket=<state bucket>" \
  -backend-config="prefix=${{ values.destination.repo }}"
terraform plan
terraform apply
```
{%- if values.enableCicd %}

### Deploy workflow

`.github/workflows/deploy.yml` plans on pull requests and applies on `main`
(job `apply`, environment `production`). It logs in with Workload Identity
Federation, without a service account key. Until the three required settings
exist it reports that and skips plan and apply.

| Setting | Kind | Content |
| ------- | ---- | ------- |
| `GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_PROVIDER` | secret or variable, required | `projects/<number>/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/<pool>/providers/<provider>` |
| `GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` | secret or variable, required | Email of the service account the workflow impersonates |
| `TF_STATE_BUCKET` | variable, required | Bucket for the Terraform state; the state prefix is the repository name |
| `FUNCTION_SOURCE_BUCKET`, `FUNCTION_SOURCE_OBJECT` | variables{% if not interpreted %}, required for `${{ runtime }}`{% endif %} | [Function package](#function-package) in Cloud Storage |
{%- if auth == 'oauth2' %}
| `OAUTH2_ISSUER`, `OAUTH2_JWKS_URI`, `OAUTH2_AUDIENCES` | variables, required | Identity provider settings |
{%- endif %}
{%- if values.enableWaf %}
| `LOAD_BALANCER_DOMAIN` | variable | Domain for the HTTPS listener |
{%- endif %}
{%- if values.enableAlarms %}
| `ALARM_EMAIL` | variable | Recipient of alert notifications |
{%- endif %}
{%- if strategy != 'all-at-once' %}
| `ROLLOUT_STEP_SECONDS` | variable | Wait between traffic steps, default 300 |
{%- endif %}

The identity provider must allow this repository
(`attribute.repository == "${{ values.destination.owner }}/${{ values.destination.repo }}"`), and the
repository's principal needs `roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser` on the service
account.
{%- endif %}

